Every smartphone is a phone. A phone can make calls, and a smartphone can make calls and take photos.
Your task:
Create a parent class phone:
init(self, br, nb) that saves self.brand and self.number a method call(self, other) that prints: is calling
Create a child class smartphone that inherits from phone: no init a new method take_photo(self) that prints: took a photo

class phone:
    
    def __init__(self, brand, number):
        self.number = number
        self.brand = brand
        
    def call(self, person):
        print(self.brand, "is calling", person)
        
class smartphone(phone):
    
    def take_photo(self):
        print(self.brand, "takes a photo")
​
obj = smartphone("iphone", "344-55")
print(obj.call("mony"))
print(obj.take_photo())
​
obj2 = phone("samsung","455-55")
print(obj2.brand)  
print(obj2.number)

