Story: Every pet has a name and an age. A cat also has a color, so the child needs to save something new. That means the child needs its own init.
Your task:
Create a parent class pet: init(self, nm, ag) that saves self.name and self.age a method info(self) that prints: is years old
Create a child class cat that inherits from pet:
its own init(self, nm, ag, cl): use super().init to save the name and age then save self.color a new method show_color(self) that prints: is

class pet():
    
    def __init__(self, name, age):
        self.name = name 
        self.age = age 
        
    def info(self):
        print(self.name, "is", self.age, " years old")
        
class cat(pet):
    
    def __init__(self, name, age, color):
        super().__init__(name, age)
        self.color = color
        
    def showcolor(self):
        print("the color of ", self.name , "is", self.color)
        
c1 = cat("bar", 46, "black")
c2 = cat("sar", 45, "grey")
​
print(c1.info())
print(c1.showcolor())
print(c1.name)
print(c2.color)

